// pc_bind_pages.inc: the rebinding pages. Data only: the F10 and Options rows list these entries in this order and
// call the pc_bind_* (pc_input.h) with the entry's scope and action. An entry at a group or ROOT reaches every
// context below it that has that action (the nearest row's keys are replaced; 'E' and 'X' rows never are), so one
// entry moves a shared action everywhere it means the same: ROOT "jump" is Space on foot, aiming, climbing, in the
// air, riding and on a vehicle. Every row of pc_scheme.inc / pc_scheme_gameplay.inc is either reached by an entry or
// listed in PC_PAGE_FIXED: tools/engine/test_pc_bind_pages.py fails otherwise, so a new row has to be placed.
//
// PC_PAGE(page, scope, action, label)     page: the F10 page; scope: a context or group of the .inc files
// PC_PAGE_FIXED(scope, action, why)        a row the player can't rebind, and why
#ifndef PC_PAGE_FIXED
#define PC_PAGE_FIXED(scope, action, why)
#endif

